<title>USA: CenCor begins self-tender at $8.75 a share.</title>
<headline>CenCor begins self-tender at $8.75 a share.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>CenCor Inc , a dissolved corporation in the process of liquidation, said Friday it began a self-tender offer for 570,000 shares of its common stock at $8.75 per share cash.</p>
<p>CenCor said the purpose of the offer is to provide shareholders who do not wish to hold shares until liquidation is completed an opportunity to sell.</p>
<p>If more than 570,000 shares are tendered, the company said it may extend the offer or increaes the number of purchased shares. The offer expires at 1800 EDT on August 5, unless extended.</p>
<p>Georgeson and Co Inc is acting as the information agent.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
